<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ceredig ap Cunedda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ceredig ap <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunedda">Cunedda</a> is the legendary founder of the early Welsh kingdom of Ceredigion, which tradition says was named after him. Welsh genealogies make him a son of Cunedda, who came from the north in the 5th century to drive Irish settlers out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, and give him the land between the rivers Dyfi and Teifi. The story was recorded centuries later and is not regarded as reliable history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ceredig-ap-cunedda.jpg" alt="Ceredig ap Cunedda" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:History_of_the_Kings_(f.96.v)_Ceredig.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
